<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="container">
    <div class="content-box hero">
        <h1>🎨 Circle Gallery 🎨</h1>
        <p>A collection of the most magnificent circles in the realm</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Famous Circles Throughout History</h2>
        
        <div class="gallery-grid">
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);"></div>
                <h3>The Original Circle</h3>
                <p>The first circle ever drawn, preserved in the Royal Archives. Legend says it was traced by the finger of Creation itself.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #ffd700 0%, #ff8c00 100%);"></div>
                <h3>The Sun Circle</h3>
                <p>Representing our sun, this golden circle illuminates all of geometry. Radius: 696,000 km of pure radiance.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #c0c0c0 40%, #808080 100%);"></div>
                <h3>The Moon Circle</h3>
                <p>A silvery circle that waxes and wanes in our perception, yet remains eternally round in reality.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0066cc 0%, #003d7a 100%);"></div>
                <h3>The Earth Circle</h3>
                <p>Our home sphere, appearing as a perfect circle from space. Equatorial radius: 6,378 km of wonder.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff0000 0%, #8b0000 100%);"></div>
                <h3>The Mars Circle</h3>
                <p>The red planet, a circular beacon in the night sky, inspiring dreams of exploration and discovery.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff69b4 0%, #ff1493 100%);"></div>
                <h3>The Cherry Blossom Circle</h3>
                <p>Nature's perfect circular petals, celebrating the beauty of mathematical precision in organic form.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Circles by Size</h2>
        
        <h3 style="margin-top: 1rem;">Microscopic Circles</h3>
        <div class="circle-display">
            <div class="circle" style="width: 20px; height: 20px; background: #e74c3c;"></div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 30px; height: 30px; background: #e67e22;"></div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: #f39c12;"></div>
        </div>
        <p>From atoms to cells, the smallest circles govern the fundamental building blocks of existence.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Human-Scale Circles</h3>
        <div class="circle-display">
            <div class="circle" style="width: 80px; height: 80px; background: #3498db;">Coin</div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 120px; height: 120px; background: #2980b9;">Plate</div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 160px; height: 160px; background: #1a5c8a;">Wheel</div>
        </div>
        <p>The circles we interact with daily, from currency to dinner plates to the wheels that transport us.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Cosmic Circles</h3>
        <div class="circle-display">
            <div class="circle" style="width: 100px; height: 100px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffd89b 0%, #19547b 100%);">🌍</div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 140px; height: 140px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fecfef 100%);">☀️</div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 180px; height: 180px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #a8edea 0%, #fed6e3 100%);">🌌</div>
        </div>
        <p>Planetary orbits, stars, and galaxies - circles that span incomprehensible distances.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Circles by Color</h2>
        
        <div class="gallery-grid">
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #ff0000;"></div>
                <h3>Passion Red</h3>
                <p>The circle of love, energy, and determination. Hot like fire, bold like courage.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #ffa500;"></div>
                <h3>Vibrant Orange</h3>
                <p>The circle of creativity and enthusiasm. Warm like sunset, inspiring like dawn.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #ffff00;"></div>
                <h3>Joyful Yellow</h3>
                <p>The circle of happiness and optimism. Bright like the sun, cheerful like laughter.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #00ff00;"></div>
                <h3>Natural Green</h3>
                <p>The circle of growth and harmony. Fresh like spring, peaceful like forests.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #0000ff;"></div>
                <h3>Tranquil Blue</h3>
                <p>The circle of calm and wisdom. Deep like ocean, vast like sky.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #800080;"></div>
                <h3>Royal Purple</h3>
                <p>The circle of nobility and mystery. Rich like royalty, enigmatic like twilight.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #ffc0cb;"></div>
                <h3>Gentle Pink</h3>
                <p>The circle of compassion and tenderness. Soft like petals, kind like care.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #000000;"></div>
                <h3>Mysterious Black</h3>
                <p>The circle of infinity and space. Deep like night, powerful like gravity.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div class="gallery-circle" style="background: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #ccc;"></div>
                <h3>Pure White</h3>
                <p>The circle of purity and possibility. Clean like snow, bright like starlight.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Special Circle Collections</h2>
        
        <h3>The Rainbow Circles</h3>
        <div class="circle-display">
            <div class="circle" style="width: 80px; height: 80px; background: linear-gradient(45deg, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet);"></div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 100px; height: 100px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, violet, indigo, blue, green, yellow, orange, red);"></div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 80px; height: 80px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet);"></div>
        </div>
        <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 1rem;">When light refracts through rain, nature paints circles in the sky with all colors of the spectrum.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem;">The Gradient Circles</h3>
        <div class="circle-display">
            <div class="circle" style="width: 100px; height: 100px; background: radial-gradient(circle, #ffffff 0%, #000000 100%);"></div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 100px; height: 100px; background: radial-gradient(circle, #ffff00 0%, #ff0000 100%);"></div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 100px; height: 100px; background: radial-gradient(circle, #00ffff 0%, #0000ff 100%);"></div>
        </div>
        <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 1rem;">Circles that demonstrate continuous transition, like sunsets and dawns, gradually changing from center to edge.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem;">The Metallic Circles</h3>
        <div class="circle-display">
            <div class="circle" style="width: 90px; height: 90px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffd700 0%, #ffed4e 50%, #ffd700 100%); box-shadow: 0 0 20px #ffd700;">Gold</div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 90px; height: 90px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #c0c0c0 0%, #e8e8e8 50%, #c0c0c0 100%); box-shadow: 0 0 20px #c0c0c0;">Silver</div>
            <div class="circle" style="width: 90px; height: 90px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #cd7f32 0%, #e09654 50%, #cd7f32 100%); box-shadow: 0 0 20px #cd7f32;">Bronze</div>
        </div>
        <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 1rem;">The circles of victory and achievement, awarded to champions throughout history.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Functional Circles in Our World</h2>
        
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>⚙️ The Gear Circle</h3>
                <div class="circle" style="width: 100px; height: 100px; background: #555; margin: 1rem auto; position: relative;">
                    <div style="position: absolute; width: 20%; height: 100%; background: #333; left: 40%;"></div>
                    <div style="position: absolute; width: 100%; height: 20%; background: #333; top: 40%;"></div>
                </div>
                <p>The foundation of mechanical engineering, transferring power through circular motion.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🎯 The Target Circle</h3>
                <div style="width: 100px; height: 100px; margin: 1rem auto; background: #ff0000; border-radius: 50%; position: relative;">
                    <div style="position: absolute; width: 70%; height: 70%; background: #fff; border-radius: 50%; top: 15%; left: 15%;"></div>
                    <div style="position: absolute; width: 40%; height: 40%; background: #ff0000; border-radius: 50%; top: 30%; left: 30%;"></div>
                    <div style="position: absolute; width: 15%; height: 15%; background: #fff; border-radius: 50%; top: 42.5%; left: 42.5%;"></div>
                </div>
                <p>Concentric circles showing precision and focus, used in sports and goal-setting.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🌊 The Ripple Circle</h3>
                <div style="width: 120px; height: 120px; margin: 1rem auto; position: relative;">
                    <div style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: rgba(52, 152, 219, 0.8); border-radius: 50%; position: absolute; top: 40px; left: 40px;"></div>
                    <div style="width: 70px; height: 70px; border: 2px solid rgba(52, 152, 219, 0.5); border-radius: 50%; position: absolute; top: 25px; left: 25px;"></div>
                    <div style="width: 100px; height: 100px; border: 2px solid rgba(52, 152, 219, 0.3); border-radius: 50%; position: absolute; top: 10px; left: 10px;"></div>
                </div>
                <p>Expanding circles that show how influence spreads outward from a central point.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Mathematical Beauty</h2>
        
        <div class="gallery-grid">
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div style="width: 150px; height: 150px; margin: 0 auto; position: relative;">
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 150px; height: 150px; background: rgba(102, 126, 234, 0.5); position: absolute;"></div>
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 150px; height: 150px; background: rgba(118, 75, 162, 0.5); position: absolute; margin-left: 50px;"></div>
                </div>
                <h3>Intersection</h3>
                <p>Two circles meet, creating the vesica piscis - a sacred geometric symbol.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div style="width: 150px; height: 150px; margin: 0 auto; position: relative;">
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 150px; height: 150px; background: transparent; border: 3px solid #667eea; position: absolute;"></div>
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 100px; height: 100px; background: transparent; border: 3px solid #764ba2; position: absolute; top: 25px; left: 25px;"></div>
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 50px; height: 50px; background: #ffd700; position: absolute; top: 50px; left: 50px;"></div>
                </div>
                <h3>Concentric</h3>
                <p>Circles sharing a center, like ripples in time or layers of wisdom.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="gallery-item">
                <div style="width: 150px; height: 150px; margin: 0 auto; position: relative;">
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 80px; height: 80px; background: #e74c3c; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 35px;"></div>
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 80px; height: 80px; background: #3498db; position: absolute; top: 60px; left: 10px;"></div>
                    <div class="gallery-circle" style="width: 80px; height: 80px; background: #f39c12; position: absolute; top: 60px; left: 60px;"></div>
                </div>
                <h3>Trinity</h3>
                <p>Three circles in perfect harmony, symbolizing balance and unity.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Virtual Circles</h2>
        <p>In the digital age, circles take on new forms:</p>
        
        <div class="info-grid">
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>💻 Loading Circles</h3>
                <p>Spinning circles that represent progress and patience in the digital realm. Their rotation soothes us while algorithms work.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>📱 App Icons</h3>
                <p>Circular badges on our devices, each a gateway to different digital worlds, arranged in perfect grids.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🎮 Game Worlds</h3>
                <p>From Pac-Man to Sonic's rings, circles have been fundamental to gaming since its inception.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>🌐 Network Nodes</h3>
                <p>Circles representing connection points in vast digital networks, enabling global communication.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box">
        <h2>Exhibition Information</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8;">
            This gallery is curated by the Royal Circle Committee and updated continuously as new circles are discovered 
            or created. Each circle in this collection has been verified for perfect roundness by the Official Geometers 
            of the realm. Visitors are encouraged to contemplate the infinite variations possible within such a simple 
            form - all defined by just one parameter (the radius), yet each unique in its expression.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 1rem;">
            <strong>Note from the Curator:</strong> "A circle is not merely a shape, but a philosophy. In its curve, 
            we see acceptance; in its center, we find focus; in its boundary, we recognize definition. May this gallery 
            inspire you to see circles not just with your eyes, but with your imagination."
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
